// =============================================================================
// winlogon-hostpools.kql - Distinct host pool names for dropdown filter
// =============================================================================
//
// WHAT IT DOES:
// Returns a list of distinct host pool names that have had connections in the
// last 7 days. Used to populate the host pool filter ComboBox in the
// Monitoring tab. Uses a 7-day window (regardless of the chart time range)
// to catch pools that might not have had connections in the last 24h.
//
// HOW IT WORKS:
// 1. Query WVDConnections for "Started" connections in the last 7 days
// 2. Extract the host pool name from _ResourceId (the 9th segment, index 8,
//    of the ARM resource path: /subscriptions/.../hostPools/{name})
// 3. Return distinct names sorted alphabetically
//
// NO PLACEHOLDERS - this query always uses a fixed 7-day window.
//
// OUTPUT COLUMNS: HostPool (string)
// =============================================================================

WVDConnections
| where TimeGenerated > ago(7d)
| where State == "Started"
| extend HostPool = tostring(split(_ResourceId, '/')[8])
| distinct HostPool
| order by HostPool asc
